{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$f_1, \\ldots, f_n \\in R$", "MATH_0003": "$R \\to R_{f_1} \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus R_{f_n}$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "MATH_0005": "$f_i$", "MATH_0006": "$R \\to R_{f_i}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-faithfully-flat-universally-injective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-cover-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9444d66b2ed29f33505cee26bca1e5e02464eee3c4b539df708ec98e20ee427c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:63784261450b12233d0eeff67e024ee539d9de27640c4572137fd798a7e07bbf", "source_text": "For a ring <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> generating the unit\nideal, the morphism <MATH_0003> is\nuniversally injective. Although this is immediate from\nLemma <REF_0001>,\nit is instructive to check it directly: we immediately reduce to the case\nwhere <MATH_0004> is local, in which case some <MATH_0005> must be a unit and so the map\n<MATH_0006> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:af88d373a738f672e894a006c440ac317fc998650772109c6c3fc2a769a259fe", "unit_id": "tag:08WN:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-faithfully-flat-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3160e0a582e5add4d95cc4d2260614af15cb4aec48a253bd4168648183c45b04", "source_text": "Any faithfully flat ring map is universally injective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6eeee1f01b8cf7e73aed202f60bf8235bd710668a3cc65138934606a317dd065", "unit_id": "tag:08WP:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-faithfully-flat-universally-injective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b14d95a8932d21a38bf498b8dfccc6c0bff96035ec9b47f6975e4b5960aa74b", "source_text": "This is a reformulation of Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a209f54629210d1197aea9b88e7b7ef2977a71fe820147d3e37a676d7f1cd2c", "unit_id": "tag:08WP:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "REF_0001": "\\cite{mesablishvili1}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c3e0e7d4a6c63f50cc1797850b72b9f53bad37521a6dbb8e058342f63fc57784", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b3ce5bb969c5da2ba14cc882744ea22b0e8cbd5b4a96aee6afdf4a232f80ab93", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe key observation from <REF_0001> is that universal injectivity \ncan be usefully reformulated in terms of a splitting, using the usual\nconstruction of an injective cogenerator in <MATH_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f77684f2fffd7071f5146846a4af5a796070aca7f4744d9ff51c99c4419b6042", "unit_id": "tag:08WJ:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$C$", "MATH_0003": "$ : \\text{Mod}_R \\to \\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nC(M) = \\Hom_{\\textit{Ab}}(M, \\mathbf{Q}/\\mathbf{Z}),\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$C(M)$", "MATH_0007": "$rf(s) = f(rs)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-C}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e08a3e9e1b0de28e71aaa6352c112b2f651af68aa3cfe1760b34eeb614553d2e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5aecb7a6ffd1043e61128430020a29d1941ae02d1cd851091eec400b9b3b6585", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring. Define the contravariant functor\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0003> by setting\n<MATH_0004>\nwith the <MATH_0005>-action on <MATH_0006> given by <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:adeed9ad3216331096015ebc80c490d601a46c1af2c4e1eca34e30df2786ef88", "unit_id": "tag:08WQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M \\mapsto M^\\vee$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-section-injectives-modules}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:048b79c7b1361649df2f8b5feb268f03dacf263571b015053cbf47ee4a599141", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a0d4f9b46baadc935e5081c654ad9823a562de192119547c5a55aee6a74b8d8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis functor was denoted <MATH_0001> in\nMore on Algebra, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:56398efaed63aa398922ddcd86567374054bd11f18baf4e8e52d5fa74d561259", "unit_id": "tag:08WJ:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$C : \\text{Mod}_R \\to \\text{Mod}_R$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-C-is-faithful}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:779209a293d4bc55ac8ef9d3d15856a77c28f64029336c5550a4fcd4a942204f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4d714a0988c75817ae77fae9ca800e0777d7d10ed65a2cf49c7cd839bab79bcb", "source_text": "For a ring <MATH_0001>, the functor <MATH_0002> is\nexact and reflects injections and surjections.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a884b38963853d99e44e7b75d3298a2650616281e42683b9528c3b55bcb03d43", "unit_id": "tag:08WR:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-vee-exact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-reflects}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6918ec44cfc2882562221f6d9a307103c3ce55dd9d715432ea8bf34fb7ed007", "source_text": "Exactness is More on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand the other properties follow from this, see\nRemark <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06016a36ed3e47e0482312bfdca79db53dfa85115a248a37a8ea0a8a38e8ada6", "unit_id": "tag:08WR:proof"}
